sts on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Derek Tran (D) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term incumbent Derek Tran defends a redrawn Orange County seat that leans about three points Democratic, against Republican Chuong Vo. Tran has raised nearly $5 million and holds a cash advantage of roughly ten to one, while Vo has raised under $1 million with little outside help. No public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on fundamentals, expert ratings, and prediction markets.\n\nRaters overwhelmingly place the race in the Likely-to-Safe Democratic column, and markets price Tran's win chances in the low-to-mid 90s. A favorable environment for Democrats adds cushion, though the seat's modest lean and Tran's narrow 2024 history keep some uncertainty. The forecast expects Tran to win by a comfortable double-digit margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 12.49}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9556, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9612, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.946, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9456, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9427, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.958, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9598, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9517, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9635, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.956, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9608, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9408, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9446, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9604, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9544, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9348, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9573, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9581, "margi